<title>CANADA: Canada agency details canola export quality.</title>
<headline>Canada agency details canola export quality.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Canadian Grain Commission on Monday detailed the quality of canola exports. All in percent of total except chlorophyl and iodine.</p>
<p>QUALITY	 SHIPPING   No1 C    No2 C    No3 C    Sample</p>
<p>Tonnes	  Aug-Oct    524,138  48,500     0	0</p>
<p>Oil	     Aug-Oct     43.1    43.2	n/s     n/s</p>
<p>Protein	 Aug-Oct     19.7    19.6	n/s     n/s</p>
<p>Chlorophyl    Aug-Oct     19	30	  n/s     n/s</p>
<p>Saturated Fat		  6.6     6.4	n/s     n/s</p>
<p>Iodine Value		 117     119	  n/s     n/s</p>
<p>Moisture	Aug-Oct	7.3     7.3	n/s     n/s</p>
<p>Waste Content Aug-Oct	2.0     2.1	n/s     n/s</p>
<p>Note: Chlorophyl is amount of mg in each kg of canola seed. Iodine value is measured in milligrams per 100 grams of oil and is a measure of unsaturated fatty acids. Oil and protein content measurements based on 8.5 percent moisture basis.</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras 204 947 3548))</p>
